why here break not continue?
This is a very common interview question. The reason is that once a substring starts with 0, making it longer will never fix the problem.

Why not continue?
If we wrote
continue

the loop would do this:

"0"    ✓
"01"   ✗
"012"  ✗

We already know
"012"

must be invalid because it still has a leading zero.
